#: src/panels/about.rs:186
msgid "The story of LieraOS"
msgstr ""

#: src/panels/about.rs:214
msgid ""
"More than thirty years ago it began with the classic distributions: SuSE, "
"Red Hat, Mandrake — tried them all, none stayed. Ubuntu was fine for a "
"while, until GNOME 3. After years of wandering I landed on Debian — and "
"stayed. Yet one question never let go: why did Debian, the foundation of so "
"many distributions, always stand on the sidelines itself?"
msgstr ""

#: src/panels/about.rs:215
msgid ""
"In my view it came down to the update philosophy. So I first built an entire "
"system from scratch — my own package manager, no base at all. It worked, but "
"it was too much for one person alone. Then I returned to Debian — not "
"because Debian was bad, quite the opposite: I still like Debian today, and "
"countless distributions rightly build upon it. I began shaping Debian into "
"what I wanted: a good mix of stability and modern software, fit for gaming "
"too, without giving up current drivers. Small changes here, my own programs "
"there — tools that work the way they should, instead of needing two programs "
"for one task."
msgstr ""

#: src/panels/about.rs:216
msgid ""
"That became a distribution: Liera — from Swedish, \"ally\", at its core a "
"Debian derivative. And because my own programs had long grown beyond a mere "
"distribution, LieraOS came to be — the entire open source world around "
"Liera: the distribution, the desktop, the tools. The OS does not stand for "
"\"Operating System\" but for Open Source. Everything is licensed under the "
"GPL."
msgstr ""

#: src/panels/about.rs:217
msgid ""
"The tools' names followed the Norse world that Liera belongs to: Ragnar, the "
"desktop. Odin, the compositor — still in the making, yet written in Rust "
"like nearly all of LieraOS; the name was pure consequence, for just as Odin "
"laid down the order of things in the myths, the compositor lays down how "
"everything appears. Valkyrie, the file manager — a name that simply belonged "
"to this world. Heimdall, guardian of the Bifröst — here guardian of the "
"network. Skald, the poet and singer of the Norse world — here for sound and "
"music. Raven, the messenger who brings word — as ravens always have."
msgstr ""

#: src/panels/about.rs:218
msgid ""
"And when the twilight of the gods comes, every error shall be counted and "
"shown."
msgstr ""

